{%- comment -%}
  Editorial band: one full-bleed photograph, a voice line and one
  underlined text link.

  On desktop the copy sits ON the LEFT HALF of the frame, over the empty-wall
  area of the editorial shot — ink on a bright surface, still no scrim (the
  thesis bans them). Below 900px the same markup falls back UNDER the picture:
  at 390px the crop leaves no empty half to print on. One DOM, two layouts
  (theme.css .home-ed__foot).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign col = section.settings.collection
  assign url = section.settings.link
  if url == blank and col != blank
    assign url = col.url
  endif

  comment
    The product picker wins over the atmosphere image — shows a model
    actually wearing a catalog piece (featured image).
  endcomment
  assign ed_img = section.settings.image
  if section.settings.image_product != blank and section.settings.image_product.featured_image != blank
    assign ed_img = section.settings.image_product.featured_image
  endif
  comment
    asset_image: landscape model shot shipped as a theme asset. A product
    featured image is 2:3 portrait and crops badly in this 3:2 slot —
    prefer a real landscape.
  endcomment

  comment
    Whether there is a picture at all decides the WHOLE layout, so it is
    resolved here, before the frame opens, rather than inside it.

    The caption is absolutely positioned against the frame and paints a
    full-width paper wash to stay readable over the photograph. With no
    picture the frame is 0px tall, so that wash and the copy both land on
    whatever section happens to sit above — measured: 354px of paper veil
    over the bottom of the category tiles, which dropped their labels to
    1.4:1 and read as a rendering fault. An unset image is a supported
    state (the merchant has not uploaded yet), so it must lay out as
    copy in normal flow, not as an overlay with nothing under it.
  endcomment
  assign ed_has_art = false
  if section.settings.asset_image != blank or ed_img != blank
    assign ed_has_art = true
  endif
-%}
<section class="home-ed bleed reveal">
  <div class="home-ed__frame{% unless ed_has_art %} home-ed__frame--bare{% endunless %}">
    {%- if section.settings.asset_image != blank -%}
      <a class="home-ed__art" href="{{ url | default: routes.all_products_collection_url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
        <img src="{{ section.settings.asset_image | asset_url }}" sizes="100vw" width="1536" height="1024" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      </a>
    {%- elsif ed_img != blank -%}
      <a class="home-ed__art" href="{{ url | default: routes.all_products_collection_url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
        <img
          src="{{ ed_img | image_url: width: 900 }}"
          srcset="{{ ed_img | image_url: width: 560 }} 560w, {{ ed_img | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w, {{ ed_img | image_url: width: 1400 }} 1400w"
          sizes="100vw"
          width="{{ ed_img.width }}" height="{{ ed_img.height }}"
          alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      </a>
    {%- endif -%}
    <div class="wrap home-ed__foot">
      {%- liquid
        comment
          Merchant copy wins in every language — the old reassign on non-primary
          locales threw it away. Both fields keep blank-means-hidden (each is
          guarded below), so there is no locale fallback: clearing them is how a
          merchant runs this section as a bare image.
        endcomment
        assign ed_caption = section.settings.caption
        assign ed_link = section.settings.link_label
      -%}
      {%- if ed_caption != blank -%}
        <p class="dl home-ed__say">{{ ed_caption | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if ed_link != blank -%}
        <a class="tlink" href="{{ url | default: routes.all_products_collection_url }}">{{ ed_link | escape }}</a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Editorial",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image", "info": "Shopify Files: brand-editorial.webp (landscape 3:2)." },
    { "type": "product", "id": "image_product", "label": "Or: product whose model photo to show", "info": "Uses the product's featured image (2:3 portrait — crops hard in this landscape slot; prefer the asset filename below)." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "asset_image", "label": "Or: theme-asset filename (wins over both)", "info": "e.g. my-image.webp — the landscape model shot shipped with the theme." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "caption", "label": "Voice line", "default": "Made for the days that don't slow down", "info": "Printed in ink on the left half of the image on desktop, under it on mobile. Keep it under ~40 characters." },
    { "type": "collection", "id": "collection", "label": "Collection" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "link", "label": "Link override", "info": "Leave empty to link to the collection." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "link_label", "label": "Link label", "default": "Shop the edit" }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Editorial",
      "settings": {
        "image": "",
        "caption": "Made for the days that don't slow down",
        "collection": "all",
        "link_label": "Shop the edit"
      }
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
